-- title:
--   Reduction at ℓ∤ N preserves integrality over the j⁻¹-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $N$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (the Mathlib algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$) satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime ℓ`, i.e. the image of $\ell$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $k_A$ for the residue field of the local ring $A$. Let $y$ be a formal Laurent series with coefficients in $A$, and write `coeffMap` for the coefficientwise application of a ring homomorphism to such a series. Assume, first, that the series $x$ obtained from $y$ by the inclusion $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N`; and, second, that $x$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subalgebra of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by $(\,\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\ \mathrm{jq})^{-1}$, the inverse of the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` $=q^{-1}\cdot$`jNumQ` of $j$. The conclusion is that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A\to k_A$ is integral over the $k_A$-subalgebra of $k_A((q))$ generated by $(\mathrm{jqModC}\ k_A)^{-1}$, where `jqModC` $k_A=q^{-1}\cdot$`jNum` reduced into $k_A$.
--
--   This is one of the two chart-wise statements expressing that good reduction of the modular curve of level $N$ at a prime $\ell\nmid N$ is compatible with integrality of $q$-expansions, here over the chart $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}[j^{-1}]$ of the $j$-line (the companion statement treats the chart generated by $j$ itself). It is used in the construction of mod $p$ modular forms from $q$-expansions, in [`ModPForms.exists_isModPCuspFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPCusp`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_isModPCuspFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPCusp) and [`ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod`](thm.html#ModPForms.exists_isModPFormFn_qexpOfWeight_eq_of_mem_modPMod).
-- source:
